# The Ashee OS build — the three things it reads from the environment.
#
# None of these is a secret and none is required: each has a default, so the build works on the
# machine it was written on with no file at all. This file exists because a value a person can
# override is a value that has to be written down somewhere a person will look —
# `system-audit.sh` section 6 asks exactly that question, and before this file the answer for
# `ASHEE_BRAND` was "nowhere".
#
# Copy to `.env` and adjust, or just export the ones you need. `.env` is gitignored; this file is
# not, which is the only reason it carries no values but the defaults.

# Where AsheeUI's shared layer lives. Required for the bundle build: the design language is read
# from that repository rather than copied into this one, because two sources of one palette drift.
# ASHEE_UI=/path/to/AsheeUI/ashee-ui/packages/shared/src

# The palette's declared source of truth, per BRAND.md.
# ASHEE_BRAND=/path/to/brand/BRAND.md

# Where `mkpendrive.sh` finds the archive it embeds. A directory, not a file.
# ASHEE_ARCHIVE=/path/to/ashee-archive
